Inference speed is paramount for real-time agent workloads because it directly impacts the responsiveness and efficiency of decision-making processes. Faster inference allows agents to process data and make decisions in real time, enabling timely responses to changing environments or user needs. In contrast, raw model quality, while essential, primarily determines the accuracy and reliability of predictions. For real-time applications where quick action is critical, speed can often be a more decisive factor than absolute model precision. Therefore, optimizing inference speed enables agents to handle high volumes of data and perform tasks swiftly, ensuring timely and effective responses in dynamic scenarios.